    "body": "## Owner checkpoint: two separate origins APPROVED AS ARCHITECTURE; offline transport implementation AUTHORIZED\n\nOwner's latest explicit instruction «хуярь» approves proceeding with the recommended **isolated private client and separate gameplay API Worker-origin topology**, and authorizes the next **offline-only** `CHAT03-TWO-PERSON-REMOTE-CLIENT-TRANSPORT` code atom. This supplements previously accepted Option A bearer auth + explicit per-device opt-in IndexedDB.\n\nSuggested naming templates, not real verified hostnames: private static client `asynchronia-chat03-client.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev`, separate gameplay API `asynchronia-chat03-gameplay.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev`, private gameplay D1 (never telemetry D1). **Only the architecture is accepted.** Exact Cloudflare account/hostnames, CSP deployment values, and resource creation/deployment remain separately gated. No Cloudflare operations, remote D1, real invite, production or main mutation approved.\n\n**Routing:** NEXT = **NEW Codex thread**, new isolated branch + Draft PR from currently verified `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558` (re-check live before writing). Source inputs: Draft #450 current `6cb4c5886f49e94240ed0b4ba133c151bc205eae` and ready/unmerged #449 `de6a6130622097d7123b3f4d6ce2da18bea1d9d3` as read-only references. No silent integration into or edits of their branches. Protect concurrent worktree and scopes; stop on collision.\n\n**Scope of new code atom:** participant-only static remote client scaffold + explicit single HTTPS API origin config (fail closed until exact owner-approved value), existing GET/commit API requests only, connection and Russian results, memory-only token default with explicit per-device IndexedDB opt-in + local Forget, secure reload/network/ambiguous-commandId retry, no raw token leakage. Synthetic offline tests; no admin routes, no client admin/recovery secrets, no real domain/deploy config, no Worker/SQL/CORS/Stage7.15/main changes. Existing local loopback harness must remain unchanged. Any actual HTTP/API integration staging, token distribution, operator readback/retention/backup, and human invitation remain separate owner-gated atoms. Lost operator replace response with unknown generation remains BLOCKED/STOP.\n\nGitHub comment is a checkpoint only and does not dispatch Codex. Notion top MEMORY_REV now `2026-10-28-CHAT03-OWNER-APPROVES-TWO-ORIGIN-CLIENT-WORK-R209`.",
